* Current-mirror TIA with PMOS gate-resistor active inductor - reconstruction
* LTspice: File > Open (All files) > this .net > Run.  Keep ptm90.lib in this folder.
* One analysis at a time: un-comment the one you want with ";" removed.
.include ptm90.lib
.temp 35

Vdd vdd 0 dc 1
Cpd in 0 450f
CL out 0 50f
Iin 0 in dc 0 ac 1
Ibp vbp 0 dc 20u
Mdp vbp vbp vdd vdd pmos90 W=2u L=200n AD=0.4p AS=0.4p PD=4.4u PS=4.4u
Cbp vbp vdd 2p
Mp1 in vbp vdd vdd pmos90 W=29.84u L=200n AD=5.968p AS=5.968p PD=60.08u PS=60.08u
M1 in in 0 0 nmos90 W=5.591u L=100n AD=1.118p AS=1.118p PD=11.58u PS=11.58u
M2 out in 0 0 nmos90 W=20.22u L=100n AD=4.044p AS=4.044p PD=40.84u PS=40.84u
Rf out in 19.217k
Ma out ga vdd vdd pmos90 W=7.568u L=100n AD=1.514p AS=1.514p PD=15.54u PS=15.54u
Rg ga out 13.553k
RL vdd out 101.51k

.ac dec 40 1Meg 100G
;.noise V(out) Iin dec 40 1Meg 100G
;.op
;Eye diagram: open the matching _eye.net file instead (transient with a PRBS7 current source).
.meas AC zt0 FIND mag(V(out)) AT 10Meg
.meas AC zpk MAX mag(V(out))
.meas AC f3db WHEN mag(V(out))=zt0/sqrt(2) FALL=1
.backanno
.end
